[{"text":"\\[\\left\\{(x(1)+x(2)+x(3)+x(4))^{2 \\varepsilon } \\left(-2 x(1) x(3) (\\text{q1}\\cdot \\;\\text{q2})-2 x(1) x(4) (\\text{q1}\\cdot \\;\\text{q2})-2 x(1) x(4) (\\text{q1}\\cdot \\;\\text{q3})-\\text{q1}^2 x(1) x(2)-\\text{q1}^2 x(1) x(3)-\\text{q1}^2 x(1) x(4)-2 x(4) x(2) (\\text{q2}\\cdot \\;\\text{q3})-2 x(1) x(4) (\\text{q2}\\cdot \\;\\text{q3})-\\text{q2}^2 x(3) x(2)-\\text{q2}^2 x(4) x(2)-\\text{q2}^2 x(1) x(3)-\\text{q2}^2 x(1) x(4)-\\text{q3}^2 x(4) x(2)-\\text{q3}^2 x(1) x(4)-\\text{q3}^2 x(3) x(4)\\right)^{-\\varepsilon -2},\\Gamma (\\varepsilon +2),\\{x(1),x(2),x(3),x(4)\\}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb15-3","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"3-loop self-energy with two massive lines","anchor":"cb15-3","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"SFAD[{{p1, 0}, {m^2, 1}, 1}, {{p2, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}, {{p3, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}, {{p2 + p3, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}, {{p1 - Q, 0}, {m^2, 1}, 1}, {{p2 - Q, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}, {{p2 + p3 - Q, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}, {{p1 + p2 + p3 - Q, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}] FCFeynmanParametrize[%, {p1, p2, p3}, Names -> x, FCReplaceD -> {D -> 4 - 2 Epsilon}]","anchor":"cb16","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{p1}^2-m^2+i \\eta ).(\\text{p2}^2+i \\eta ).(\\text{p3}^2+i \\eta ).((\\text{p2}+\\text{p3})^2+i \\eta ).((\\text{p1}-Q)^2-m^2+i \\eta ).((\\text{p2}-Q)^2+i \\eta ).((\\text{p2}+\\text{p3}-Q)^2+i \\eta ).((\\text{p1}+\\text{p2}+\\text{p3}-Q)^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb16-5","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"An example of using FCFeynmanParametrize together with FCFeynmanParameterJoin","anchor":"cb16-5","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"props = {SFAD[{p1, m^2}], SFAD[{p3, m^2}], SFAD[{{0, 2 p1 . n}}], SFAD[{{0, 2 (p1 + p3) . n}}]}","anchor":"cb17","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{(\\text{p1}^2-m^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{(\\text{p3}^2-m^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{(2 (n\\cdot \\;\\text{p1})+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{(2 (n\\cdot (\\text{p1}+\\text{p3}))+i \\eta )}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb17-2","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"intT = FCFeynmanParameterJoin[{{props[[1]] props[[2]], 1, x}, props[[3]] props[[4]], y}, {p1, p3}]","anchor":"cb18","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{(\\left(-x(1) m^2-x(2) m^2+\\text{p1}^2 x(1)+\\text{p3}^2 x(2)\\right) y(1)+2 (n\\cdot \\;\\text{p1}) y(2)+(2 (n\\cdot \\;\\text{p1})+2 (n\\cdot \\;\\text{p3})) y(3)+i \\eta )^4},6 y(1),\\{x(1),x(2),y(1),y(2),y(3)\\}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb18-2","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"Here the Feynman parameter variables x_i and \\(y_i\\) are independent from each other, i.e. we have \\delta(1-x_1-x_2-x_3) \\times \\delta(1-y_1-y_2-y_3). This gives us much more freedom when exploiting the Cheng-Wu theorem.","anchor":"cb18-2","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"FCFeynmanParametrize[intT[[1]], intT[[2]], {p1, p3}, Indexed -> True, FCReplaceD -> {D -> 4 - 2 ep}, FinalSubstitutions -> {SPD[n] -> 1, m -> 1}, Variables -> intT[[3]]]","anchor":"cb19","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{y(1) \\left(x(1) x(2) y(1)^2\\right)^{3 \\;\\text{ep}-2} \\left(y(1) \\left(x(1) x(2)^2 y(1)^2+x(1)^2 x(2) y(1)^2+x(2) y(2)^2+x(1) y(3)^2+x(2) y(3)^2+2 x(2) y(2) y(3)\\right)\\right)^{-2 \\;\\text{ep}},\\Gamma (2 \\;\\text{ep}),\\{x(1),x(2),y(1),y(2),y(3)\\}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"In the case that we need U and F polynomials in addition to the normal output (e.g. for HyperInt)","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"(SFAD[{{0, 2*k1 . n}}]*SFAD[{{0, 2*k2 . n}}]*SFAD[{k1, m^2}]* SFAD[{k2, m^2}]*SFAD[{k1 - k2, m^2}]) out = FCFeynmanParametrize[%, {k1, k2}, Names -> x, FCReplaceD -> {D -> 4 - 2 Epsilon}, FCFeynmanPrepare -> True]","anchor":"cb20","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{k1}^2-m^2+i \\eta ) (\\text{k2}^2-m^2+i \\eta ) ((\\text{k1}-\\text{k2})^2-m^2+i \\eta ) (2 (\\text{k1}\\cdot n)+i \\eta ) (2 (\\text{k2}\\cdot n)+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb20-5","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"From this output we can easily extract the integrand, its x_i-independent prefactor and the two Symanzik polynomials","anchor":"cb20-5","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"{integrand, pref} = out[[1 ;; 2]] {uPoly, fPoly} = out[[4]][[1 ;; 2]]","anchor":"cb21","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{(x(3) x(4)+x(5) x(4)+x(3) x(5))^{3 \\varepsilon -1} \\left(m^2 x(3) x(4)^2+m^2 x(3) x(5)^2+m^2 x(4) x(5)^2+m^2 x(3)^2 x(4)+m^2 x(3)^2 x(5)+m^2 x(4)^2 x(5)+3 m^2 x(3) x(4) x(5)+n^2 x(2)^2 x(3)+n^2 x(1)^2 x(4)+n^2 x(2)^2 x(4)+2 n^2 x(1) x(2) x(4)+n^2 x(1)^2 x(5)\\right)^{-2 \\varepsilon -1},-\\Gamma (2 \\varepsilon +1)\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb21-3","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{x(3) x(4)+x(5) x(4)+x(3) x(5),m^2 x(3) x(4)^2+m^2 x(3) x(5)^2+m^2 x(4) x(5)^2+m^2 x(3)^2 x(4)+m^2 x(3)^2 x(5)+m^2 x(4)^2 x(5)+3 m^2 x(3) x(4) x(5)+n^2 x(2)^2 x(3)+n^2 x(1)^2 x(4)+n^2 x(2)^2 x(4)+2 n^2 x(1) x(2) x(4)+n^2 x(1)^2 x(5)\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb21-3","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"Symbolic propagator powers are fully supported","anchor":"cb21-3","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"SFAD[{I k, 0, -1/2 + ep}, {I (k + p), 0, 1}, EtaSign -> -1] v1 = FCFeynmanParametrize[%, {k}, Names -> x, FCReplaceD -> {D -> 4 - 2 ep}, FinalSubstitutions -> {SPD[p] -> 1}]","anchor":"cb22","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(-k^2-i \\eta )^{\\text{ep}-\\frac{1}{2}}.(-(k+p)^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb22-4","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{(-x(1)-x(2))^{3 \\;\\text{ep}-\\frac{7}{2}} x(2)^{\\text{ep}-\\frac{3}{2}} (-x(1) x(2))^{\\frac{3}{2}-2 \\;\\text{ep}},\\frac{(-1)^{\\text{ep}+\\frac{1}{2}} \\Gamma \\left(2 \\;\\text{ep}-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{\\Gamma \\left(\\text{ep}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)},\\{x(1),x(2)\\}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb22-4","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"An alternative representation for symbolic powers can be obtained using the option SplitSymbolicPowers","anchor":"cb22-4","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"SFAD[{I k, 0, -1/2 + ep}, {I (k + p), 0, 1}, EtaSign -> -1] v2 = FCFeynmanParametrize[%, {k}, Names -> x, FCReplaceD -> {D -> 4 - 2 ep}, FinalSubstitutions -> {SPD[p] -> 1}, SplitSymbolicPowers -> True]","anchor":"cb23","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(-k^2-i \\eta )^{\\text{ep}-\\frac{1}{2}}.(-(k+p)^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb23-4","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{x(2)^{\\text{ep}-\\frac{1}{2}} \\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{2} (1-2 \\;\\text{ep})+\\frac{1}{2} (4-2 \\;\\text{ep})-1\\right) x(1) (-x(1)-x(2))^{3 \\;\\text{ep}-\\frac{7}{2}} (-x(1) x(2))^{\\frac{1}{2}-2 \\;\\text{ep}}+\\left(2 \\;\\text{ep}+\\frac{1}{2} (2 \\;\\text{ep}-1)-3\\right) (-x(1)-x(2))^{3 \\;\\text{ep}-\\frac{9}{2}} (-x(1) x(2))^{\\frac{3}{2}-2 \\;\\text{ep}}\\right),\\frac{(-1)^{\\text{ep}+\\frac{1}{2}} \\Gamma \\left(2 \\;\\text{ep}-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{\\Gamma \\left(\\text{ep}+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)},\\{x(1),x(2)\\}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb23-4","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"Even though the parametric integrals evaluate to different values, the product of the integral and its prefactor remains the same","anchor":"cb23-4","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"Integrate[Normal[Series[v1[[1]] /. x[1] -> 1, {ep, 0, 0}]] /. x[1] -> 1, {x[2], 0, Infinity}] Normal@Series[v1[[2]] %, {ep, 0, 0}]","anchor":"cb24","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{2}{5}\\]","anchor":"cb24-3","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{4 i}{15}\\]","anchor":"cb24-3","section":"Feynman representation"},{"text":"Integrate[Normal[Series[v2[[1]] /. x[1] -> 1, {ep, 0, 0}]] /. x[1] -> 1, {x[2], 0, Infinity}] Normal@Series[v2[[2]] %, {ep, 0, 0}]","anchor":"cb25","section":"Feynman representation"}]